{"decision":{"id":"track-storage","about":"How does Class.track(instance)/Class.instances() remember instances — a plain array or a WeakRef set?","options":[{"id":"array","say":"A plain array, push on track()","why":"Simplest possible code, no GC subtlety."},{"id":"weakref","say":"A Set of WeakRefs, instances() drops dead ones on read","why":"Several classes here build throwaway instances that live one render and are dropped (Page.drew_content()'s own copy, content_at()'s preview Page) — a plain array would hold every one of those forever and only grow."}],"chose":"weakref","because":"Page is the first real user and Page instances are built throwaway in several places already (drew_content, content_at); a WeakRef set means the tracked list is always what is actually still alive, never a leak, at the cost of one extra Set/WeakRef per class (core/track/track.js).","rule":"code#9-oop-a-default-view-for-any-instance","status":"open"}}
{"decision":{"id":"track-location","about":"Where does the one-line-per-class tracking mechanism live — a tiny function each class calls once, or a mixin/base class other classes extend?","options":[{"id":"function","say":"core/track/track.js exporting track(Klass) — call track(Page) once, then Page.track(this) in the constructor","why":"Opt-in per class, one import, one call; a class that never calls it pays nothing and appears in no registry."},{"id":"mixin","say":"A Trackable base class, or track()/instances() built straight onto View so every View has it","why":"Nothing to import per class — but every View (and everything built on it) would track by default, which the brief explicitly rules out (\"don't make every class track by default\")."}],"chose":"function","because":"The requirement is opt-in per class; a shared base or a View-level default would make tracking the default instead of the exception, and most classes here should show up in no instances() list at all.","rule":"code#9-oop-a-default-view-for-any-instance","status":"open"}}
