{"review":{"at":"2026-09-29T17:37:37-05:00","size":"full","verdict":"fix","findings":[{"n":1,"kind":"fix","text":"The phone measurement has only a BEFORE run. requirements.md asks for before and after, and measure/task.jsonl stops at \"waiting for the AFTER instruction\". Run the AFTER on the card page (Fast 3G), and land with both numbers side by side."},{"n":2,"kind":"fix","text":"The BEFORE diagnostic (measure/task.jsonl) found that the phone waits on about 150 small requests, not on bytes. The new readers add requests: Markdown.js `walk()` (depth Infinity, one page.jsonl per folder) and ext/files/fs.js `list()` fetch a log for every sub-folder, so /fs/ or an md index on a big folder can mean hundreds or thousands of requests where there used to be one directory.json. Measure one big folder (for example /framework/ext/files/fs/ pointed at /framework/) before calling this a phone win, or cap the depth."},{"n":3,"kind":"note","text":"The review/shots/ folder is empty: none of the listed sheet.png files exist. So nothing here judges layout, order or navigation from pictures. The readers minion says its headless probe of 8 pages showed 0 directory.json fetches and 0 console errors. That is the only visual evidence."},{"n":4,"kind":"note","text":"The covered-folder rule (Server/plugins/PageFiles.js:124-141) still covers `assets/` and `img/` folders (public/assets/page.jsonl, public/assets/img/page.jsonl, ai2/doc/img/page.jsonl), which the brief suggested leaving out. The result is 2,407 new tracked files. The rule was applied without being shown to the owner as a proposal, even though the brief named \"don't clutter the tree\" as the concern."},{"n":5,"kind":"note","text":"From now on, creating any file under public/ appends a line to a git-tracked page.jsonl. Every new file therefore shows up as two changes in git. `merge=union` (.gitattributes:13) handles merges, but the noise in diffs and commits is new, and the owner should know about it."},{"n":6,"kind":"note","text":"The line format is not the one in requirements.md: it writes `{\"file\":\"kid/\"}` instead of `{\"dir\":\"kid\"}`, and `{\"file\":\"x\",\"gone\":true}` instead of `{\"removed\":\"x\"}`. Reusing the existing format is the simpler choice, and core/Page/doc/jsonl.md documents it, but say so in the landing report so it doesn't read as a missed ask."},{"n":7,"kind":"note","text":"The Router's child lookup (core/Page/Page.class.js:225-240) only uses a listing that something else has already fetched (`loaded_listing`). It never fetches one itself, so requirement 4 is only partly met for the Router. The comment gives a reason (every folder would pay a fetch), and that reason is fair, but name it in the report."},{"n":8,"kind":"note","text":"PageFiles now appends file lines to folders that have a page.js, including imagine/cms/json/page.jsonl, whose log is also the CMS's own page data (jsonl.md, \"A folder with a page.js is no longer skipped\"). That works only while the CMS reader keeps ignoring `file` lines. It is worth a one-line check that /imagine/cms/json/ still renders and saves."},{"n":9,"kind":"note","text":"dev/DevBar/ask.js:62-81 and ext/drawer/tabs/sessions.js:27-45 now hold the same new `threads()` body, line for line. The simpler way is one exported function (sessions.js already exports it) that ask.js imports."},{"n":10,"kind":"note","text":"ai2/groups.js `day()` (line ~379) turns every folder in a day into a Member and calls `live()` on its task.jsonl, even folders with no task.jsonl. Before this change, only folders with a task.jsonl were read. This is harmless over the socket, but each empty folder is a wasted subscription. Filtering on the folder's own listing when it is already loaded would cost nothing."},{"n":11,"kind":"note","text":"The earlier readers review (readers/review.md #1: a log with no `file` lines is read as an empty folder, not as \"no listing\") is mostly moot now that the backfill has caught up every existing log. The comment on `listing()` at core/Page/Log.js:492 still says so plainly, so that one is fine as it stands."}],"branch":"worktree/page-files-log","head":"d9bec9ca16533246576fdda764da46ee3659e730","model":"claude-opus-5-5","cost":2.3028411999999996,"file":"review.md"}}
