{"decision":{"at":"2026-09-30T22:40:00Z","topic":"deliverable 1 - measure edge","text":"Added border-inline-end: 1px solid var(--line) plus padding-inline-end to ai2.css's existing measure rule (:is(.ai2-full-card, .ai2-card-tabs > .tab-panel) > :is(.ai2-text, .ai2-refined, .ai2-summary, .ai2-tally, p)), giving the reading column a visible edge instead of removing the cap.","alternative":"let the prose fill (max-width: none) instead of bordering it. Rejected: the measure is a deliberate reading-width choice elsewhere on this page; the owner offered both options and a visible edge keeps that intent legible."}}
{"decision":{"at":"2026-09-30T22:41:00Z","topic":"deliverable 2 - the 500px void","text":"Root cause found by driving the real page with Playwright and reading getComputedStyle(pageEl).gridTemplateColumns directly. ai2.css's @media (width>=40em) rule reserved a SECOND grid column (minmax(0,1fr) var(--ai2-chat, max(18rem,33.333%))) for the card's bottom chat (.ai2-foot), which Card.V1=false (default since 2026-09-29, doc/one-ai.md) no longer renders on most cards. Measured exactly 437.328px reserved for nothing at 1920 with the drawer at its default open width -- 33.333% of the 1312px page, matching the owner's 'about 500 pixels' closely. Fixed by adding :has(> .ai2-foot) to the media-query selector, so the existing one-column rule (2026-09-24, 'ONE COLUMN, THE WHOLE WIDTH') wins for every ordinary card.","alternative":"the coordinating mastermind's own hypothesis (framework.css's --rail-floor push clamp) was checked and ruled out empirically -- at normal widths it never engages; the real bug had nothing to do with the drawer's own push math."}}
{"decision":{"at":"2026-09-30T22:42:00Z","topic":"deliverable 3 - click-to-select","text":"ext/drawer/select.js's DrawerSelect.active() was tabs.mine() alone -- true whenever the drawer was open on its own tabs, so ANY click not matching the short OWN_CLICK list (native buttons/links/inputs) read as select-this, including ext/Dropdown's <summary> trigger for the card's Actions menu. Gated active() on an explicit inspect-mode html class, added as a checkbox in the drawer's Settings tab using the exact check()/knob() mechanism dev-outline (x-ray) already uses -- off by default, persists across reload like dev-outline. Turning it off also clears any live hover/selection via the checkbox's changed callback.","alternative":"widen OWN_CLICK to also exclude [role=button]/<summary>/etc. Rejected: treats symptoms one selector at a time and a future custom control reopens the same bug; the owner asked by name for an inspect-mode toggle."}}
