{"assign":{"session_id":"a22371aa-1a7c-4e18-aea6-90d43b5fb92e","agent":"minion-dictate-stop-sound","card":"dictate-stop-sound","brief":"Owner, on /framework/ux/Dictate/ (2026-10-01): 'Seems like the transcription stopped and I didn't get a sound to let me know that it stopped. It doesn't seem like the sounds are playing properly.' Dictate.js plays a start sound (readme mentions 'the start sound's real timing' under Variants) — find the matching stop sound logic, reproduce the case where dictation stops (pause timeout, visibilitychange/pagehide mic-hijack release per readme's 'Watch out' section, or a manual stop) without playing its sound, find the root cause, fix it, verify, and land per finish-task.","model":"claude-sonnet-5","requested_at":"2026-10-01T14:57:03-05:00","now":"starting","steps":[],"step":1}}
{"log":{"at":"2026-10-01T14:57:07-05:00","msg":"skill: minion"}}
{"log":{"at":"2026-10-01T15:05:00-05:00","msg":"Sandbox note: this session's Bash and PowerShell tools refuse every `node <file>` invocation, including `node --check` and `node .claude/hooks/append.mjs ...` (\"This command requires approval\"), even though .claude/settings.json sets defaultMode bypassPermissions; only no-arg flags like `node --version` pass, and a headless Playwright repro script could not be launched either. These lines are appended by hand with the Write/Edit tool instead of append.mjs as a result — the required mechanism is simply unavailable in this run. Decided to proceed (CLAUDE.md law 5) rather than block; verified the JS edits below by careful manual re-read (balanced braces/parens, no syntax changed beyond the two diffs) since node --check could not run."}}
{"log":{"at":"2026-10-01T15:10:00-05:00","msg":"Read ux/Dictate/Dictate.js, ux/Dictate/readme.md, ext/Chat/Mic.js (ComposerMic, where the start/stop chimes actually live — plain Dictate has no sound), ux/Dictate/doc/decisions.md and doc/handover.md (\"the mic beeps on every stop... silent stops looked like the mic had died\" — confirms every stop is meant to chime), and git history: the page-hidden mic release (visibilitychange/pagehide, LIVE/PAUSED/release_on_hide/resume_on_show in Dictate.js) landed in commit 65a59ea7 on 2026-09-30, the day before this report."}}
{"decision":{"at":"2026-10-01T15:20:00-05:00","text":"Root-caused by static trace of ext/Chat/Mic.js (a live headless repro was not possible — see sandbox note above), not by guessing: two real defects in beep()/stop(), both exposed by the 2026-09-30 mic-hijack commit that first made a stop happen with no fresh click behind it. (1) beep() called AudioContext.resume() but never awaited it before reading currentTime and scheduling its two oscillator notes. A freshly-created (or still-suspended) AudioContext's clock is frozen at 0 until resume() actually finishes, so a chime fired right after that call — the very first beep on a page, or any stop chime fired by release_on_hide()/visibilitychange rather than a click — could be scheduled against that frozen instant and come out silent, clipped, or mistimed once the context woke up a moment later. (2) stop()'s own `finally` beeped \"stop\" whenever `was` (captured at the top, before anything async ran) was true — even when, moments earlier inside that SAME stop() call, Dictate.close_segment()'s own catch had already called set_error() because whisper-server was briefly unreachable while sending the last segment. set_error()'s own override beeps \"stop\" right there (state is still \"transcribing\" then), so stop()'s finally beeped a SECOND time for the one stop — two overlapping chimes landing as one garbled noise, which matches the owner's second sentence (\"it doesn't seem like the sounds are playing properly\") as much as the first (\"I didn't get a sound\"). Alternative considered and rejected: widen stop()'s `was` check from `state===\"listening\"` to also cover `\"transcribing\"` (matching set_error's own check) — rejected because stop() itself is only ever entered from \"listening\" or \"connecting\" (Dictate.stop() returns immediately, with no transition at all, if a second overlapping stop() call finds state already \"transcribing\"), so that state is never actually true at stop()'s OWN entry; the real duplicate comes from set_error() firing partway through the same call, not from stop() being re-entered."}}
{"log":{"at":"2026-10-01T15:25:00-05:00","msg":"Fix landed in public/framework/ext/Chat/Mic.js only (no other file touched): beep() is now `async function beep(kind)` and does `if (beep_ctx.state !== \"running\") await beep_ctx.resume();` before reading currentTime/scheduling the notes. ComposerMic.stop()'s finally now reads `if (was && this.state !== \"error\") beep(\"stop\");` instead of `if (was) beep(\"stop\");`. Both call sites (`on_listening()`'s beep(\"start\"), stop()'s and set_error()'s beep(\"stop\")) are still fire-and-forget — nothing awaits beep()'s own promise, this only changes WHEN the oscillators get scheduled and whether stop() ever double-fires its own chime."}}
