{"assign":{"step":1,"landed_at":"2026-10-01T15:34:00-05:00","title":"✦ sheet + Chrome's toolbar auto-hide: researched, documented, not built","outcome":"**No code changed — a researched, documented answer.**\n- [x] find the sheet's real scroll structure — `position: fixed` (the whole sheet, even at full height) wrapping a second, separate `overflow-y: auto` thread inside it — doc/sheet.md\n- [x] is a nested scroll area the blocker — no: the site's own ordinary pages already scroll through a nested div too (`.pages`) and Chrome hides its toolbar on that fine; the real wall is `position: fixed` plus a thread that never fills the whole screen by itself — doc/sheet.md\n- [x] say whether a fix is possible — yes on paper (make the thread the one full-screen scroller, pin the head/composer inside it with `position: sticky`, hide `.pages` while full) — not built: no headless tool anywhere can render Chrome's own address bar, so there is no way to prove such a rewrite actually works, and it is real surgery on a part of the sheet that had three regressions land today already","links":[{"url":"/framework/ext/drawer/doc/sheet/","label":"doc/sheet.md — the full finding and the fix recipe"},{"url":"/framework/ext/drawer/","label":"ext/drawer"}],"tokens":null,"note":"window/tokens omitted — the usage-check script hit the same approval wall this session could not grant (see the log line above); this task's own spend is small: research plus one doc edit, no fan-out."}}
