l setup work with nothing built yet to demo or measure against.","then":[]},{"id":"both-now","text":"Build Voice.Browser and a stubbed Voice.Local side by side immediately, same split as Transcriber from day one.","say":"Build Voice.Browser and a stubbed Voice.Local side by side immediately, same split as Transcriber from day one.","caveats":["a Local engine with no binary to run against is guesswork, not working code — Transcriber itself only grew its Whisper engine once whisper-server actually existed to build and measure against."],"caveat":"a Local engine with no binary to run against is guesswork, not working code — Transcriber itself only grew its Whisper engine once whisper-server actually existed to build and measure against.","then":[]}],"recommended":"browser","confidence":0.85,"why":"Matches the brief's own words — \"browser SpeechSynthesis API for a zero-dependency start\" — and mirrors Transcriber's own history: Transcriber.Browser shipped first because it needs nothing installed, Transcriber.Whisper came later once whisper-server existed to wrap. Voice can grow a Voice.Local the same way, the day the owner picks and installs a local TTS engine; building that wrapper now, with nothing to run it against, would be unmeasured guessing. Law 1 (fastest working version first) and law 6 (don't build a second system before the first one's proven) both point the same way.","sources":["public/framework/audio/readme.md","public/framework/audio/Transcriber/Browser.js","public/framework/audio/Transcriber/Whisper.js","public/framework/audio/doc/decisions.md","Server/plugins/Whisper.js","grep of Server/ for tts|speech|piper|coqui|espeak (no local TTS plugin found)"],"depends_on":null,"status":"decided","decided_by":"system","owner_only":null,"by":"minion-voice-tts","at":"2026-10-01T15:45:00-05:00"}}
